# Let Celebrate admins record Stripe invoice IDs on payments

byre task tskxBsNBsDoEIW, "Celebrate invoice IDs", created by ian@fc.run, merged by ian@fc.run.
Full transcripts: the events of task tskxBsNBsDoEIW in byre (GET /api/events?task_id=tskxBsNBsDoEIW).

## Summary

Celebrate admins had no way to record the Stripe invoice that bills a payment: no policy let anyone but a super admin set `PAYMENT.stripe_invoice`, and the Payments tab showed it only as text.

- **Policy:** `(set PAYMENT.stripe_invoice (admin_of "celebrate"))` in `internal/db/policy.go`.
  Before: only super admins could set `stripe_invoice`.
  Now: Celebrate admins can too.
- **Page:** on Celebrate's admin Payments tab (`web/celebrate/pages/admin.js`), each payer with owed (blank-status) rows in the filtered view has a Record invoice button. It opens a box with an `in_…` ID field and one toggle per owed row, all on, and writes `stripe_invoice` and `status=requested` to the picked rows in one batch.
- **Decisions:**
  - Recording an invoice also marks its rows Requested, since sending the invoice is asking for the money.
  - One toggle per row, because an invoice can bill only some of a payer's rows.
  - Only owed rows are offered, so an ID already recorded is never overwritten.
- **Docs:** `docs/datamodel.md`, `docs/celebrate/data.md` and `docs/celebrate/celebrate.md`.
- **Test:** `TestCelebrateAdminsRecordTheInvoiceThatBillsAPayment` in `internal/db/celebratewrites_test.go`.
- **Checking:** the page was viewed on a local, read-only snapshot of production data as ian, then the snapshot was deleted. Saving from the box wasn't clicked through; the server side of that write is covered by the test.
- **Left out:** a way to edit the invoice ID on a row already Requested. Setting the row back to Owed puts it back under Record invoice.

